<article class="env-remark" id="0EJC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EJC">Remark <span data-tag="0EJC">52.20.7</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring which has a dualizing complex and is complete with respect to $f \in \mathfrak m$. Let $(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ be an object of $\textit{Coh}(U, f\mathcal{O}_ U)$ where $U$ is the punctured spectrum of $A$. Set $Y = V(f) \subset X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. If for $y \in U \cap V(f)$ closed in $U$, i.e., with $\dim (\overline{\{ y\} }) = 1$, we assume the $\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge $-module $\mathcal{F}_ y^\wedge $ satisfies the following two conditions </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}_ y^\wedge [1/f]$ is $(S_2)$ as a $\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge [1/f]$-module, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $\mathfrak p \in \text{Ass}(\mathcal{F}_ y^\wedge [1/f])$ we have $\dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, y}^\wedge /\mathfrak p) \geq 3$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $(\mathcal{F}_ n)$ is the completion of a coherent module on $U$. This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/0EJ9" data-tag="0EJ9">52.20.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0EJA" data-tag="0EJA">52.20.5</a>. </p>
</article>